menu "K-FSW platform"

config KFSW_STORAGE
	bool "K-FSW filesystem storage lifecycle"
	depends on FLASH_MAP
	depends on FILE_SYSTEM_LITTLEFS
	depends on FILE_SYSTEM_MKFS
	help
	  Enable the K-FSW LittleFS storage lifecycle over the fixed flash
	  partition selected by the kfsw,storage-partition devicetree chosen
	  property. File operations continue to use Zephyr's filesystem API.

config KFSW_WATCHDOG
	bool "K-FSW hardware watchdog"
	depends on WATCHDOG
	help
	  Enable the platform watchdog mechanism: arm the device selected by
	  the kfsw,watchdog devicetree chosen property, keep it fed, and allow
	  the feed to be stopped so that the part resets.

	  This is the mechanism only. It carries no health policy and decides
	  nothing about whether the system is well.

	  On a target with no kfsw,watchdog chosen node the API is still
	  present and every operation reports -ENODEV, so a composition without
	  watchdog hardware builds and runs unchanged.

config KFSW_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Watchdog timeout in milliseconds"
	depends on KFSW_WATCHDOG
	default 8000
	range 100 32000
	help
	  Time the hardware allows between feeds before resetting the part.
	  The keep-alive feeds at a third of this, so two consecutive feeds can
	  be missed before a reset. The upper bound is what the STM32
	  independent watchdog can express from its low-speed oscillator.

config KFSW_WATCHDOG_AUTO_START
	bool "Arm the watchdog during application start-up"
	depends on KFSW_WATCHDOG
	default y
	help
	  Arm the hardware once the application has finished bringing services
	  up. Turn this off to arm it explicitly, which is what a composition
	  wants when a later boot stage decides whether the image is healthy
	  enough to guard.

endmenu
